From f3dcf789be5dc970338bbd9ad229012680298a00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calvin Hill <calvin@hakobaito.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 22 May 2019 11:23:37 +0000
Subject: Initial support for Node.js

Rebased onto v22.23.3:
- os.cpus(): dropped the change that commented out GetCPUInfo and left
  os.cpus() returning undefined. libuv 1.51+ implements uv_cpu_info() for
  Haiku, and many npm packages call os.cpus().length.
- ResetSignalHandlers(): instead of commenting out both sigaction() checks
  (which read an uninitialized struct and skipped every reset), skip only
  the signal numbers Haiku rejects and keep resetting the rest.
- common.gypi/configure.py/node.gypi/node_report.cc/rand_unix.c: same
  changes, moved to new anchors (openharmony was added to the OS lists,
  max_memory_size_kbytes became max_memory_size_bytes, OpenSSL 3.5 restyle).

